{
 "key": "st.sam-yot",
 "as_of": null,
 "guide": {
  "lead": {
   "en": "Sam Yot is the old town's quiet rail corner — an underground Blue-line station beneath Charoen Krung at the Sam Yot junction, straddling Phra Nakhon, Pom Prap Sattru Phai and Samphanthawong. The Khlong Ong Ang promenade (Friday-Sunday walking street, kayaks, street art) runs beside the station, and listings put 11,000-13,000 THB studios and 14,000-15,000 THB 1-bedrooms at the door. The trade-offs: safety 5 has no visible unit-specific basis, evening life is event-driven rather than street-level, and the district's registered population is shrinking. Purple Line interchange targeted November 2030.",
   "claims": [
    "sam-yot-c07",
    "sam-yot-c13",
    "sam-yot-c15",
    "sam-yot-c16",
    "sam-yot-c14"
   ]
  },
  "sections": {
   "strengths": [
    {
     "en": "Khlong Ong Ang promenade — restored moat canal, verified inside the catchment — gives daily waterside walking plus a Fri-Sun 16:00-22:00 walking street.",
     "claims": [
      "sam-yot-c07"
     ]
    },
    {
     "en": "Market density (Trok Mo dawn market, Khlong Thom, Mega Plaza) supports daily_essentials 9 for a car-free household.",
     "claims": [
      "sam-yot-c13"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "tradeoffs": [
    {
     "en": "Safety 5 has no visible unit-specific evidence base — only generic old-town night emptiness after ~22:00 and the tourist-fringe scam genre.",
     "claims": [
      "sam-yot-c15"
     ]
    },
    {
     "en": "Vibe 10 / nightlife 9 are event- and heritage-driven: the 17 small bars and the Fri-Sun walking street carry it, and the canal's revival has stagnated between festivals.",
     "claims": [
      "sam-yot-c16"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "dayNight": [
    {
     "en": "Daytime is a government-office and market quarter; evenings depend on the Fri-Sun walking street and small bars, with backstreets dim after ~22:00.",
     "claims": [
      "sam-yot-c14"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "variation": [
    {
     "en": "The station quarter (Wang Burapha, Dinso) differs from the canal-frontage blocks and from the Pom Prap and Samphanthawong fringes the catchment touches.",
     "claims": [
      "sam-yot-c02"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "fit": [
    {
     "en": "Poor fit: park-dependent households — Rommaninat Park computes outside the catchment (st.sanam-chai side) despite facing Exit 1.",
     "claims": [
      "sam-yot-c10"
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  "uncertainties": [
   "safety 5: No unit-specific evidence for the 5 was found in EN or TH sources; keep the rating but pair it with an explicit 'basis: generic old-town night emptiness + tourist-friction genre; nothing local documented' note. The quarter has a staffed MRT station, government offices and a park open to 21:00 — a plain safety deficit is not evidenced. Recommend the app label this rating low-confidence for this unit.",
   "vibe 10 + nightlife 9 with 17 venues: Vibe 10 is defensible as heritage identity (three-peaked-gate story, tone-controlled streets, adaptive reuse) plus event evenings; nightlife 9 with 17 mapped venues only makes sense as small in-unit bars plus immediate access to Chinatown's Soi Nana and the old-town tourist edge. State that mechanism explicitly; do not imply a club district.",
   "green 9: Supported by Rommaninat Park (free, to ~21:00, fitness/skate/basketball) and the always-open canal promenade; caveat that the 4.4 ha park figure is app-only (BMA page 403) and walking-street operation on the canal is intermittent — the promenade, not the market, is the dependable green asset. | Coordinator correction 2026-11-07: Rommaninat Park computes OUTSIDE the catchment polygon (st.sanam-chai side); the in-unit green case rests on Khlong Ong Ang, temple and institutional grounds.",
   "rent 8: Listings corroborate the blend: 11,000-13,000 THB studios steps from the station, 14,000-15,000 THB 1BR condos, 20,000 THB aged shophouse; whole-shophouse asks are much higher, so 'cheap' applies to rooms and small units. Portal asks, not transacted rents.",
   "daily_essentials 9: Market density is real (dawn wet markets, market malls, 553 food venues); the soft spot is hospitals — none verified inside the unit, nearest general hospitals several km. Consider reflecting that in the essentials narrative rather than the score.",
   "crowd 2 / transport 7: Crowd 2 matches shrinking registered population (Wang Burapha 10,414 to 8,344, 2019-2025) and a daytime-office swell pattern. Transport 7 matches MRT+bus strength, no BTS, and car-priority streets between station and Dinso (2025 pilot programme exists)."
  ],
  "attribution_required": []
 },
